# CODEOWNERS - the people who must approve a change to the files that judge a
# change. Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace @your-github-user with a
# person's GitHub user name or an @org/team of people. Never a bot: a bot's
# approval is not a person deciding.
#
# GitHub reads the first of .github/CODEOWNERS, CODEOWNERS and docs/CODEOWNERS
# that exists, and the last matching pattern wins. Keep these lines LAST, so no
# later pattern takes one of these files away from its owner, and never leave a
# pattern under them with no owner: that leaves its files approvable by anyone
# with write access.
#
# This file does nothing by itself. Branch protection (or a ruleset) on the
# default branch must "Require review from Code Owners"; see
# references/stage-3-6-build.md, "Approval rules for an agent-authored change".
# scripts/check-approval-rules.py reads this file; it cannot read the settings.

/.claude/productizer/ @your-github-user
/.github/workflows/ @your-github-user
